# Practice sudoers.d (~/sysroot/etc/sudoers.d)
#
# Write one file per delegation here, e.g. a file named "deploy" containing:
#
#   deploy ALL=(ALL) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/systemctl restart app
#
# Rules of the craft:
#   - one file per purpose, named after the user or role (never edit sudoers itself)
#   - least privilege: name exact commands, never ALL unless you mean it
#   - mode 0440 (root-readable only) — sudo refuses to read anything else
#   - ALWAYS validate with: visudo -c -f <file>  (look for "parsed OK")
#
# On a real host this directory is /etc/sudoers.d and you edit as root.
# Here it lives in the practice root because the container is unprivileged.
